# The font map: which font file draws each font name of werkkzeug's Text operator.
#   name = font file | the sentence said in every caption
# The file is taken relative to this map's folder. Point WZ_FONTMAP at your copy of this file.
# An empty font name in a graph is "arial": werkkzeug3's own rule (FontBegin in _start.cpp).
# Arial, Times New Roman and Verdana are Microsoft's and are not shipped here. These lines name free fonts
# (Debian: fonts-liberation, fonts-dejavu-core); a person who has the named fonts points the lines at them.
arial = LiberationSans-Regular.ttf | Liberation Sans 2.1.5 stands in for Arial (metric-compatible)
times new roman = LiberationSerif-Regular.ttf | Liberation Serif 2.1.5 stands in for Times New Roman (metric-compatible)
verdana = DejaVuSans.ttf | DejaVu Sans 2.37 stands in for Verdana (not metric-compatible: its letters are a different width)
